@startuml deployment
' ============================================================================
' Sunrise Dental Clinic — Deployment Diagram (pure Java)
'
' One WAR, three tiers inside it, deployed to a standalone Tomcat. Evidence
' for the "distributed application with web services" requirement is the
' /api/* endpoint family: reachable over HTTP independently of any browser
' session, returning JSON, exactly as a client other than this project's own
' JSP pages could call it.
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam node {
    BorderColor #0F6E7E
    BackgroundColor #F7F9F9
    FontColor #12313A
}
skinparam artifact {
    BorderColor #5D7D87
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
skinparam database {
    BorderColor #0F6E7E
    BackgroundColor #E4F0F1
}
skinparam note {
    BorderColor #B5701F
    BackgroundColor #FBEEDD
}

actor "Reception desk\nstaff" as User

node "Client workstation" as Client {
    artifact "Web browser" as Browser
}

node "Application server\n(Apache Tomcat 11)" as AppServer {
    artifact "sunrise-dental.war" as War {
        component "JSP views\n(presentation)" as Views
        component "Servlets: /api/*\n(web services)" as ApiServlets
        component "Servlets: /*\n(JSP-rendering)" as WebServlets
        component "AuthenticationFilter" as Filter
        component "Service layer\n(business logic)" as Services
        component "DAO layer\n(JDBC)" as Daos
    }
}

node "Database server" as DbServer {
    database "MySQL 9.0\nsunrise_dental" as DB {
        artifact "Tables + constraints" as Tables
        artifact "sp_daily_revenue" as Proc
        artifact "trg_appointment_status_audit" as Trigger
    }
}

User --> Browser
Browser --> Filter : HTTP\nport 8080
Filter --> WebServlets : session-authenticated
Filter --> ApiServlets : session-authenticated
WebServlets --> Views
WebServlets --> Services
ApiServlets --> Services
Services --> Daos
Daos --> DB : JDBC\nMySQL Connector/J, port 3306

note right of ApiServlets
  Returns JSON with no dependency on the JSP
  views. This is the web-service surface: a
  client other than this project's own pages
  could call POST /api/appointments directly
  over HTTP and get the same JSON contract,
  proven in the test plan by
  AppointmentApiServletTest and by curl.
end note

note right of Filter
  Default-deny across the whole application,
  with an explicit allow-list for /login,
  /logout, /css, /js and /favicon.ico. A page
  added later is protected unless someone
  deliberately exempts it.
end note

note bottom of DB
  Constraints, the audit trigger and the
  revenue procedure live with the data, so
  they hold regardless of which servlet
  issued the query.
end note

@enduml
